{
  "title": "Catalogue benchmark, 2026-09-11 (audit API-03, round 2)",
  "method": "scripts/bench/catalog-bench.mjs --sizes 100,1000 --time-budget 1800: disposable catalogues of N synthetic apps under the system temp directory, 4 php -S workers (separate processes contending for the catalogue flock), 8 requests in flight; phases list and read (200 requests each), publish and update (50 each), mixed (200: half list, three tenths read, one tenth run count, one tenth patch). \"before\" measured a copy of apps/softn-api as of commit 7f1ea46 (--api <copy>), 16:17-16:29 local; \"after\" the working tree with the round-2 repair (change-based bundle-cache revalidation with a bounded periodic sweep; the slug-keyed catalogue built once per request and handed to every card), 18:47-18:51 local. No other catalogue benchmark ran during either (tasklist checked). Latency is measured by the client around fetch; lock wait, lock hold, boot, rebuild and commit are the API's own Server-Timing. The 10,000-app size was not run: the session was closed before the capped run started.",
  "caveats": [
    "The \"before\" JSON the script wrote was overwritten by another agent's benchmark that used the same scratch file name; \"before\" here is parsed from the run's printed table (the same numbers, without the per-phase max lock/hold columns), which is why its shape is slightly narrower than \"after\".",
    "Another agent's Studio micro-benchmark (vitest bench, single process) finished at 18:46:22, seconds before the \"after\" run began; the first seconds of its 100-app build may have overlapped that tail. The 1,000-app \"after\" phases ran alone.",
    "A clean sequential rerun of both was started at 18:52 and stopped at 18:54 at the coordinator's request; its completed part (100 apps, all phases, \"before\") is included as cleanRerunBefore and agrees with \"before\" within noise (list p50 156 vs 160 ms).",
    "Both runs used the same fixtures, ports, worker count and machine; other agents' editors and unit-test runs in the same session were the only other load."
